 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DexFblEh9o7/",
 "title": "How to be remembered after networking events",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator suggests avoiding the common phrase 'it was nice meeting you' because it makes you forgettable. Instead, use a two-line method involving a memorable label and a trigger tied to future events so people introduce you to others.",
 "key_points": [
  "Never say 'It was nice meeting you' because everyone says it and you become just another face.",
  "Swap your closing for two lines where the second one gets you introduced to people you haven't met yet.",
  "Line one is the label: phrase it like a joke, for example, 'You're gonna remember me as the agency guy who also hates these events.'",
  "Line two is the trigger: tie yourself to something that is going to happen anyway, like 'Next time you meet someone starting a business, send them my way.'",
  "Leave first while the conversation is still good, not when it is dying, so people want more of whoever left at the high point."
 ],
 "content": "Leave first. Say your two lines while the conversation is still good, not when it’s dying. People want more of whoever left at the high point. Follow, my networking playbook drops soon. #networking #socialskills #entrepreneur",
